                {menSizes.map(r => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="primary-cell"><strong>US {r.us.toFixed(1)}</strong></td>
                    <td class="highlight-cell"><strong>India {r.india.toFixed(1)}</strong></td>
                    <td>EU {r.eu}</td>
                    <td>{r.cm.toFixed(1)} cm</td>
                    <td>{r.inch.toFixed(1)}"</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Women's Table -->
        <div class="table-panel" id="tab-women" role="tabpanel">
          <h3 class="table-heading">Women's US to India Shoe Size Chart</h3>
          <div class="table-wrapper">
            <table class="size-table" aria-label="Women US to India shoe size chart">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>US Women Size</th>
                  <th>India Size (UK)</th>
                  <th>EU Size</th>
                  <th>Foot Length (CM)</th>
                  <th>Inches</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {womenSizes.map(r => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="primary-cell"><strong>US {r.us.toFixed(1)}</strong></td>
                    <td class="highlight-cell"><strong>India {r.india.toFixed(1)}</strong></td>
                    <td>EU {r.eu}</td>
                    <td>{r.cm.toFixed(1)} cm</td>
                    <td>{r.inch.toFixed(1)}"</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Kids' Table -->
        <div class="table-panel" id="tab-kids" role="tabpanel">
          <h3 class="table-heading">Kids' & Youth US to India Shoe Size Chart</h3>
          <div class="table-wrapper">
            <table class="size-table" aria-label="Kids US to India shoe size chart">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>US Kids Size</th>
                  <th>India Kids Size</th>
                  <th>EU Size</th>
                  <th>Foot Length (CM)</th>
                  <th>Age Stage</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {kidsSizes.map(r => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="primary-cell"><strong>US {r.us}</strong></td>
                    <td class="highlight-cell"><strong>India {r.india}</strong></td>
                    <td>EU {r.eu}</td>
                    <td>{r.cm.toFixed(1)} cm</td>
                    <td>{r.stage}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Editorial SEO Prose Section -->
    <article class="editorial-band">
      <div class="page-inner prose-article">
        <h2 class="editorial-main-title">How to Convert US Shoe Size to India: Complete Sizing Guide</h2>
        
        <p class="lead-paragraph">
          Navigating international footwear sizing can be a source of confusion for online shoppers ordering <strong>branded shoes in india</strong> or importing luxury sneakers from American retailers. Understanding the exact <strong>shoe size of us and india</strong> is essential to getting a comfortable fit on the first try. Because India adheres to the British UK sizing system for length measurements, American shoe sizes do not correspond directly to Indian numbers. This comprehensive guide breaks down the mathematical conversion rules, brand idiosyncrasies, and regional fit nuances so you can seamlessly <strong>convert us shoe size to india</strong>.
        </p>

        <h3>Core Rules to Convert Shoe US Size to India</h3>
        <p>
          The fundamental conversion between the American scale and an <strong>indian shoe size chart</strong> hinges on gender categories. While both standards rely historically on the 1/3-inch (barleycorn) scale, their baseline starting points differ:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Men's Footwear (India = US − 1):</strong> For adult men, Indian shoe sizes run exactly 1 full number smaller than American sizes. If you wear an American men's size 9, your Indian equivalent is size 8 (fitting an anatomical footbed of 27.0 cm). If you are looking up <strong>us8 size in india</strong>, an American US 8 translates directly to an Indian size 7 (26.0 cm, EU 41).</li>
          <li><strong>Women's Footwear (India = US − 2):</strong> Because the American women's system begins three full numbers earlier than the men's scale, the difference on a <strong>women shoe size chart india</strong> is 2 full sizes. A woman wearing an American US 7 corresponds to an Indian size 5 (24.0 cm, EU 38), and an American US 8 translates to an Indian size 6 (25.0 cm, EU 39).</li>
          <li><strong>Kids' Footwear:</strong> For toddlers and children, American sizes are generally 0.5 to 1 size larger than Indian sizes (e.g., US 10C child corresponds to Indian 9.5C, approximately 16.5 cm).</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Understanding the India Footwear Size Chart & Standards</h3>
        <p>
          For decades, the standard <strong>india footwear size chart</strong> has mirrored British lasts. However, nationwide anthropometric research conducted by the Council of Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR-CLRI) revealed that Indian feet are distinctly wider at the ball, arch, and metatarsal joints compared to traditional European or American lasts. In response, the Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) introduced the "Bha" footwear sizing framework, providing wider forefoot proportions for enhanced orthopedic comfort.
        </p>
        <p>
          When shopping on Indian e-commerce giants such as Myntra, Flipkart, Ajio, or Tata CliQ, size dropdowns frequently offer selections in UK/India, US, and EU formats. Consulting an accurate <strong>foot size chart in india</strong> enables you to cross-check foot length in centimetres (CM) against the manufacturer's specific cut.
        </p>

        <h3>Branded Shoes in India vs. Domestic Shoe Companies</h3>
        <p>
          The Indian footwear ecosystem features a vibrant mix of prominent domestic manufacturers and leading global athletic giants:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Domestic Giants (Bata, Liberty, Relaxo, Campus, Red Tape):</strong> Leading <strong>shoes companies india</strong> like Bata India, Relaxo (Sparx), Campus Activewear, Paragon, and Red Tape manufacture directly according to Indian/UK numbering. If you wear an Indian size 8 in Bata formal shoes, you will require a US size 9 when shopping for American dress shoes or boots.</li>
          <li><strong>International Athletic Brands (Nike, Adidas, Puma, Skechers):</strong> Global sportswear labels print US, UK, and EU measurements on the interior tongue tag. For instance, a Nike Men's US 10 box will list UK 9, which represents an Indian size 9 (28.0 cm). Skechers and New Balance follow identical labeling structures.</li>
          <li><strong>Converse and Canvas Sneakers:</strong> Converse All Star Chuck Taylors feature unisex American sizing that can surprise Indian shoppers. To verify your fit in person, many sneaker enthusiasts visit an official <strong>converse shoes store in delhi</strong>—such as branches in DLF Promenade Vasant Kunj, Select Citywalk Saket, or flagship stores in Connaught Place—or renowned multi-brand <strong>shoe stores delhi</strong> throughout Karol Bagh and South Extension.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Cracking Common European Sizing Queries in India</h3>
        <p>
          Because many European fashion houses (such as Zara, H&M, Mango, and Marks & Spencer) operate extensively across Indian metropolitan malls and e-commerce platforms, Indian shoppers frequently search for European size translations:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Euro 37 size in india:</strong> Corresponds to Indian size 4 to 4.5 (fitting a 23.5 cm footbed), equivalent to an American US Women 6.5.</li>
          <li><strong>38 size in india shoes:</strong> European 38 translates to Indian size 5 for women (fitting a 24.0 cm footbed), which equals an American US Women 7.</li>
          <li><strong>Euro size 40 in india / 40 size in india shoes:</strong> Corresponds to Indian size 6 to 6.5 for men (US Men 7–7.5, 25.5 cm) or Indian size 6.5 to 7 for women (US Women 8.5–9).</li>
          <li><strong>42 size shoe in india:</strong> European 42 equals Indian size 8 for men (fitting a 27.0 cm footbed), which corresponds to an American US Men 9.</li>
          <li><strong>43 shoe size in india:</strong> European 43 equals Indian size 9 for men (fitting a 28.0 cm footbed), which maps to an American US Men 10.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>How to Measure Your Foot Size at Home Using an Indian Chart</h3>
        <p>
          To ensure 100% sizing accuracy when ordering across borders, measure your anatomical foot length using this simple three-step method:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>Place a blank sheet of paper firmly on a flat, hard floor against an uncarpeted wall.</li>
          <li>Stand on the sheet with your heel lightly touching the wall, wearing the socks you plan to use with the footwear. Mark the furthest tip of your longest toe with a pencil held vertically.</li>
          <li>Measure the distance from the back edge of the paper to your pencil mark in centimetres. Match this metric number directly against our <strong>foot size chart in india</strong> above to discover your exact US, Indian, and European shoe size.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- FAQ Accordion Section -->
    <section class="faq-band">
      <div class="page-inner">
        <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions: US to India Sizing</h2>
